title: 'pallet-revive: fix eth_getLogs with empty address/topic filter lists'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    An `eth_getLogs` filter with an empty address list (`"address": []`) or an empty topic
    list at a position (`"topics": [[]]`) built an `IN ()` SQL clause. SQLite evaluates
    `IN ()` as always-false, so the filter silently returned zero logs. Such filters are
    valid Ethereum requests: an empty list is a wildcard that matches any value. An empty
    address list now matches any address, and an empty topic list matches any value at that
    position while still requiring the topic to exist — so, as in go-ethereum, a filter of
    length N only matches logs with at least N topics.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: patch
